Source: nostr-faucet
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: DWDC <apt@dwdc.club>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc, pkgconf, libssl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: nostr-faucet
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: ask a signet miner for coins over Nostr
 An NWC wallet service implementing pay_bip321, on-chain branch, backed by a
 bitcoind wallet rather than a Lightning node. A client sends a BIP-321
 bitcoin: URI and the miner pays it.
 .
 One instance per miner. Each holds RPC to exactly one bitcoind and serves
 exactly one chain, so a request for one chain cannot be paid from another's
 miner and the RPC connection never leaves the machine.
 .
 The service dials out to a relay and never listens on a port, so installing
 it beside a miner adds nothing to that host's firewall.
 .
 This process can spend the wallet it is pointed at. It runs as its own
 unprivileged user, and its payouts are bounded by a per-key quota, a request
 rate limit, and a total cap that is refused even to a key inside its own
 quota.
